					<description><![CDATA[<p>Long before your toddler picks up a pencil, they're building the hand strength and control writing requires. Art is a playful way to get there. From water painting to drawing on a vertical easel, the Play Every Way Table encourages grip, finger precision, and wrist control that lay handwriting's foundation.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://blog.lovevery.com/learning-cognitive-skills/how-toddler-art-helps-build-fine-motor-skills-for-handwriting/">How toddler art helps build fine motor skills for handwriting</a> appeared first on <a href="https://blog.lovevery.com">Lovevery</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										
					
